  "goodToKnow": "Der Treibstoff is fuel, for engines, rockets and planes; the official term for cars is der Kraftstoff, and in everyday speech, Sprit or Benzin and Diesel. At German petrol stations, Super E10 contains 10 percent ethanol. Figuratively, Treibstoff can be what drives something: Kaffee ist mein Treibstoff. Treiben means to drive or propel. Plural: die Treibstoffe."
